    /// Adds a processor. You can add a processor to migrate event data to the cloud. You can preset the
    /// implementation of the processor on the device and set its properties based on its constraints. Note that the
    /// configuration information of **Processor** must be provided by the data processor. Yet, as no data processor is
    /// preset in the device for interaction for the moment, migrating events to the cloud is unavailable.
    ///
    /// # Arguments
    ///
    /// * `processor` - Pointer to the processor, that is, the pointer returned by [`OH_HiAppEvent_CreateProcessor`](crate::hiappevent::OH_HiAppEvent_CreateProcessor).
    ///
    /// # Returns
    ///
    /// - Unique ID if set is successful. The value is greater than 0.
    /// - [`HIAPPEVENT_PROCESSOR_IS_NULL`](crate::hiappevent::HiAppEvent_ErrorCode::HIAPPEVENT_PROCESSOR_IS_NULL): The **processor** parameter is empty.
    /// - [`HIAPPEVENT_INVALID_PARAM_VALUE`](crate::hiappevent::HiAppEvent_ErrorCode::HIAPPEVENT_INVALID_PARAM_VALUE): Invalid parameter value.
    /// - [`HIAPPEVENT_OPERATE_FAILED`](crate::hiappevent::HiAppEvent_ErrorCode::HIAPPEVENT_OPERATE_FAILED): Failed to find or register the data processor name.
    /// - [`HIAPPEVENT_INVALID_UID`](crate::hiappevent::HiAppEvent_ErrorCode::HIAPPEVENT_INVALID_UID): Invalid user ID.
    ///
    /// For details, see [`HiAppEvent_ErrorCode`](crate::hiappevent::HiAppEvent_ErrorCode).
    ///
    /// Available since API-level: 18
    #[cfg(feature = "api-18")]
    #[cfg_attr(docsrs, doc(cfg(feature = "api-18")))]
    pub fn OH_HiAppEvent_AddProcessor(processor: *mut HiAppEvent_Processor) -> i64;
    /// Destroys a processor. Note: If a processor is no longer used, destroy it to release memory to prevent memory
    /// leaks. After the processor is destroyed, set its pointer to null.
    ///
    /// # Arguments
    ///
    /// * `processor` - Pointer to the processor, that is, the pointer returned by [`OH_HiAppEvent_CreateProcessor`](crate::hiappevent::OH_HiAppEvent_CreateProcessor).
